(%      endx    : the ending value for x)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(%      starty  : the initial value)Tj
T*
(%      func    : routine name to calculate the right hand )Tj
T*
(%                side of the D.E..  This must be specified)Tj
T*
(%                as a string.)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%   ex: [x,y] = eulerApprox\(0,1,1/16,1,'f'\);)Tj
T*
(%       Will return the approximation of a D.E.)Tj
T*
(%       where x is from 0 to 1 in steps of 1/16.)Tj
0 -1.20001 TD
(%       The initial value is 1, and the right hand)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(%       side is calculated in a subroutine given by)Tj
T*
(%       f.m.)Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%  The routine will generate two vectors.  The first)Tj
T*
(%  vector is x which is the grid points starting at)Tj
T*
(%  x0=0 and have a step size h.  )Tj
T*
(%)Tj
T*
(%  The second vector is an approximation to the specified)Tj
T*
(%  D.E. )Tj
T*
(%)Tj
0 -4.8 TD
(x = [startx:h:endx];)Tj
0 -2.40001 TD
(y = 0*x;)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(y\(1\) = starty;)Tj
0 -2.39999 TD
(for i=2:max\(size\(y\)\),)Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(   y\(i\) = y\(i-1\) + h*feval\(func,x\(i-1\),y\(i-1\)\);)Tj
T*
(end)Tj
